{"id": "P00137", "name": "Gennady Timchenko", "name_chinese": "季姆琴科", "country": "Russian Federation", "net_worth_usd_m": "24165.6", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Oil; gas", "industry": "energy", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2008-2025); Hurun Global (2014-2026); Wikidata (2019)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/gennady-timchenko/", "wikidata_url": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1502398", "forbes_bio": ["Gennady Timchenko has stakes in various Russian businesses, including gas company Novatek and petrochemical producer Sibur Holding.", "Timchenko ran a state-owned oil exporting company and became one of its largest shareholders when it was later privatized.", "One of Russia's most powerful people, he befriended Putin in the 1990s in Saint Petersburg when he and the Rotenberg brothers started a judo club called Yavara- Neva.", "Timchenko was sanctioned by the U.S. in 2014 and by the EU and U.K. in 2022.", "He remains chairman of the Russian national hockey league KHL and is president of the SKA Saint-Petersburg Hockey Club."], "forbes_facts": ["Timchenko grows apples in Russia.", "Timchenko sold his stake in trading company Gunvor to partner Torbjorn Tornqvist in 2014, a day before he was hit with sanctions."]}
{"id": "P01167", "name": "Gordon Getty", "name_chinese": "戈登·盖蒂", "country": "United States", "net_worth_usd_m": "5754.9", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Getty Oil", "industry": "energy", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2001-2025); Hurun Global (2014-2026); Wikidata (2025)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/gordon-getty/", "wikidata_url": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3110901", "forbes_bio": ["Gordon Getty, whose oil tycoon father J. Paul died in 1976, led the sale of his family's Getty Oil to Texaco for $10.1 billion in 1984.", "Once the sole trustee of the family trust, Getty orchestrated the breakup into six separate trusts in 1985.", "Getty is a classical music composer, whose compositions include the Canterville Ghost, Plump Jack and Usher House.", "Since 2008, Getty has given more than $450 million to his philanthropic foundation, which supports performing arts, music and museum projects.", "He founded PlumpJack Winery in 1995 with Gavin Newsom, now California's governor."], "forbes_facts": ["An opera and wine aficionado, Getty is a partner in Odette Estate winery in Napa Valley.", "The Getty family faced many tragedies: The wife of Gordon's brother J. Paul Jr. died of a heroin overdose and J. Paul Jr.'s son was kidnapped by Italian gangsters.", "Getty has publicly acknowledged the fact that he has two families: four sons with his late wife Ann, and three daughters with Cynthia Beck."]}
